    "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nWith `--context-parallel-size 1`, the Megatron Qwen3.5-VL path cannot complete a\r\ntraining step: any packed sequence with an odd token count is rejected before\r\nthe first optimizer step. `examples/geo3k_vlm/run_geo3k_qwen35.sh` sets CP 1, so\r\nthe example ships in that state.\r\n\r\nThis PR makes `_inject_vision_embeddings()` skip the CP→packed index mapping\r\nwhen there is no CP group, which is the same condition `gather_packed_input_ids()`\r\nalready short-circuits on. One file, no behaviour change for `cp_size > 1`.\r\n\r\n## The bug\r\n\r\n```\r\nFile \"slime_plugins/models/qwen3_5_vl.py\", line 163, in _inject_vision_embeddings\r\n    local_indices = get_packed_cp_local_indices(\r\nFile \"slime_plugins/models/qwen3_5_vl_utils.py\", line 22, in get_packed_cp_local_indices\r\n    raise ValueError(f\"Packed sequence length {sequence_length} must be divisible by 2 * CP size {cp_size}\")\r\nValueError: Packed sequence length 4551 must be divisible by 2 * CP size 1\r\n```\r\n\r\n`get_packed_cp_local_indices()` maps a CP rank's local tokens back to the packed\r\nstream through Megatron's two-chunk zigzag layout, which splits every sequence\r\ninto `2 * cp_size` chunks — hence the divisibility requirement. The check is\r\ncorrect for that layout, but `_inject_vision_embeddings()` calls the helper\r\nunconditionally, passing `cp_size=1` when no CP group exists. At `cp_size=1` the\r\nrequirement degenerates into \"every packed sequence must have an even length\".\r\n\r\nPacked lengths are whatever the micro-batch happens to pack, so about half of\r\nthem are odd. A run therefore survives until the first odd pack and then dies\r\ninside `train_one_step`.\r\n\r\n## Reproduction\r\n\r\n* Model `Qwen/Qwen3.5-35B-A3B`, `examples/geo3k_vlm` (GEO3K), Megatron training\r\n  backend, `--colocate`, `TP2 / PP1 / CP1`.\r\n* Observed on 1 node × 8 GPUs at EP8 and on 2 nodes × 16 GPUs at EP16 alike —\r\n  the failure does not depend on the parallel layout, only on CP being 1.\r\n* Rollout 0 generates normally; the job fails ~140 s into the first\r\n  `train_one_step`, at whichever micro-batch first packs to an odd length.\r\n\r\nAny VL run with `--context-parallel-size 1` and packed sequences reproduces it;\r\nno images or dataset specifics are required beyond taking the vision-injection\r\npath.\r\n\r\n## The fix\r\n\r\n```python\r\nif cp_group is None or cp_group.size() == 1:\r\n    local_indices = None\r\nelse:\r\n    local_indices = get_packed_cp_local_indices(\r\n        cu_seqlens, cp_group.size(), cp_group.rank(), input_ids.device\r\n    )\r\nlocal_feature_indices = feature_indices if local_indices is None else feature_indices[local_indices]\r\n...\r\n\r\n\r\nWhy this is the identity case, not a suppressed check:\r\n\r\n* `forward()` builds `full_input_ids` with `gather_packed_input_ids()`, which\r\n  returns `input_ids` unchanged when the CP group is `None` or of size 1. So at\r\n  CP 1 the full packed stream and the local stream are the same tensor.\r\n* `feature_indices` is built over `full_input_ids`, i.e. already in local order,\r\n  and `feature_indices[arange(n)] == feature_indices`.\r\n* Where the helper previously succeeded at `cp_size=1` (even lengths), it\r\n  returned exactly that identity range — first half of each sequence followed by\r\n  its second half. No output that used to be produced changes.\r\n\r\nThe token-layout assertion right below the change is kept and still runs: at\r\nCP 1 both sides have the same length, so it remains a meaningful check.\r\n\r\n## Why the call site rather than the helper\r\n\r\n`get_packed_cp_local_indices()` and its divisibility check are left untouched.\r\nThe check describes a real constraint of the two-chunk layout that function\r\nimplements; what is wrong is asking it for a mapping when no CP split exists.\r\nFixing the caller keeps the helper's contract intact and matches the\r\nshort-circuit `gather_packed_input_ids()` already performs for the same\r\ncondition.\r\n\r\n## Scope and risk\r\n\r\n* `slime_plugins/models/qwen3_5_vl.py` only, +18 / −7.\r\n* `cp_size > 1` takes exactly the same path as before.\r\n* `tests/test_qwen3_5_vl_native.py::test_thd_cp_indices_select_two_chunks_per_packed_sequence`\r\n  covers the helper at `cp_size=2` and is unaffected.\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n\r\n* Existing unit tests are untouched and still describe the `cp_size > 1` layout.\r\n* Verified end to end by rerunning the GEO3K configuration above, which\r\n  previously stopped at the `ValueError` in the first training step.\r\n* No unit test is added for the CP-1 path: it lives in\r\n  `_inject_vision_embeddings()`, which needs a constructed `Qwen3_5VLModel`\r\n  (Megatron parallel state, a vision tower and an embedding layer), which the\r\n  current pure-`torch` test module cannot build. Happy to add one if you would\r\n  prefer the fix inside `get_packed_cp_local_indices()` instead, where it is\r\n  directly unit-testable.\r\n",
