    {
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "I hit the same error with Qwen3.5-0.8B at slime 41014d1, on 2 GPUs with TP 1 and CP 1:\r\n\r\n```\r\nValueError: Packed sequence length 1109 must be divisible by 2 * CP size 1\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt failed in the first training step. The failing sample was text-only, so a micro-batch with no image fails too. About half of the samples have an odd length: 5198 of 10240 in my 40-step 0.8B run.\r\n\r\nCPU reproduction on main `05e3b017`. It needs only `torch` and slime:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npython -c \"import torch; from slime_plugins.models.qwen3_5_vl_utils import get_packed_cp_local_indices as f; f([0, 1109], 1, 0, torch.device('cpu'))\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nI used the helper-side variant that the description offers at the end. It returns `torch.arange(boundaries[0], boundaries[-1], device=device)` when `cp_size == 1`. Results:\r\n\r\n- With it, 40 training steps ran on Qwen3.5-0.8B and on Qwen3.5-2B, both with TP 1 and CP 1.\r\n- On CPU, the output is the same as on main for even lengths at CP 1 (500 random cases), and for all ranks at CP 2, 4 and 8 (1400 cases). Bad lengths still raise at CP > 1.\r\n- `tests/test_qwen3_5_vl_native.py`: 8 passed on main `05e3b017` with the change.\r\n\r\nWith the helper-side variant, this pure-`torch` test covers CP 1. It fails on main and passes with the change:\r\n\r\n```python\r\n@pytest.mark.unit\r\ndef test_thd_cp_indices_are_identity_without_cp():\r\n    indices = get_packed_cp_local_indices([0, 3, 4, 7], cp_size=1, cp_rank=0, device=torch.device(\"cpu\"))\r\n    assert indices.tolist() == list(range(7))\r\n```\r\n\r\nI did not run the call-site version in this PR. It covers the same case. `examples/geo3k_vlm/run_geo3k_qwen35.sh` uses CP 1, so merging either version would let the example train.",
